    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i dont think i have the energy for \"small moments\" or \"stepping back\" anymore. it's just... constant. it's like a low hum of misery that never stops. everything feels so pointless when you realize you're just a stranger to everyone else, even yourself. sometimes i just wonder if there's even a point to continuing the struggle if the destination is just more of the same. like, why keep trying to find a place when the whole world feels so wrong?\n Balance the weight of all feels impossible.  greco- style,",
      "source": "evaluator",
